From fbd536dbe0066f1b627f08bf2ecb4034b53dedc8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Z User <z@container>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 19:47:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Consolidate f4-scenario-player into f4-world-viewer
 (--scenario mode)

The standalone f4-scenario-player executable is merged into the world
viewer as a third top-level mode (alongside Campaign and Replay). The
scenario player's Simulation/Scenario/terrain/camera/overlays now live
in a self-contained ScenarioPlayerState on ViewerApp::Impl, mirroring
the existing ReplayState pattern.

What's saved (the duplicated code this removes):
  - A whole CMake target + its raylib/imgui FetchContent wiring
  - A second Raylib+ImGui init/shutdown boilerplate (InitWindow,
    rlImGuiSetup, SetTargetFPS, the main loop, rlImGuiShutdown,
    CloseWindow) -- the scenario now uses the viewer's single loop
  - A second RenderResources instance (the heaviest GPU resource: the
    glTF model cache, lit shader, texture cache) -- the scenario now
    BORROWS impl.render_res_3d
  - A second screenshot path, a second terrain-load path

What's kept (scenario-specific, owned by ScenarioPlayerState):
  - Its own Simulation + Scenario (separate from the campaign session)
  - Its own TerrainData/TerrainMesh + textured-theater WorldView
  - Its own aircraft-scale OrbitCamera (1..100k ft, 250 ft initial)
  - Its own AirfieldOverlays + RadioLog + CombatTranscript + missile trails
  - Its in-frame fixed-timestep tick loop (vs V-CAMP's worker thread)
  - The headless --harness BVR-intercept QC path (run_harness, no GL)

New files in f4-world-viewer:
  src/scenario_player_state.hpp   -- ScenarioPlayerState struct
  src/scenario_player_view.cpp    -- load/run/draw logic (ported from the
                                     former player_app.cpp + renderer.cpp)
  src/airfield_overlays.cpp       -- moved (namespace f4::viewer)
  src/radio_log.{hpp,cpp}         -- moved (namespace f4::viewer)
  scenarios/*.json.in             -- moved (18 templates)

CLI: f4-world-viewer --scenario <path> [--run] [--follow] [--speed x]
    [--record qc/<name>/trace.json] [--screenshot out.png]
    [--harness out.json] [--camera-distance ft] [--width/--height N]
The flags mirror the former f4-scenario-player CLI 1:1.

The world viewer's run() gains a third dispatch branch; the campaign
session/FairMutex/bubble blocks are gated on !scenario_player.active()
just as they already are on !replay.active(). The shared scheduled-
screenshot path gains an exit-after-screenshot for scenario mode.
